\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar keeps healthy tone on stocks, rate cut talk. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Carolyn Cohn \par \uc2 553 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 August 2002\par 14:17\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Aug 7 (Reuters) - The dollar held its ground near recent six-week peaks against the euro and the yen on Wednesday, cushioned by increasing expectations of an asset-boosting U.S. rate cut and by talk of U.S. funds bringing money home. \par \par \uc2  U.S. blue-chip stocks rose by nearly three percent on Tuesday, and futures pointed to a higher open on Wednesday, on mounting speculation that the Fed would trim rates by the end of the year. \par \par \uc2  Such a move would boost the U.S. economy and U.S. stocks, and therefore the dollar, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  "After yesterday's big move, people are waiting to see which direction the dollar is going to take," said Lee Ferridge, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Rabobank. \par \par \uc2  "They are looking to see how the Dow opens, and futures have been doing well this morning." \par \par \uc2  The dollar was trading at 120.52/54 yen at 1150 GMT, slightly down from the U.S. close and a little more than half a yen below six-week highs set on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The dollar eased off against the euro, dropping a third of a percent from the U.S. close to approach $0.97, compared with six-week highs of $0.9619 also set on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The dollar's recent strong performance follows months of weakness for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and for U.S. stock markets, and analysts said the dollar has benefited from U.S. investment shifts back into U.S. assets. \par \par \uc2  "U.S. assets are quite cheap, and that's when people start picking them up," said David Bloom, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at HSBC Markets. \par \par \uc2  U.S. equities got an additional boost in after-hours trading after networking giant Cisco Systems posted higher quarterly earnings in after-hours trade. \par \par \uc2  GERMAN JITTERS \par \par \uc2  The euro brushed off data showing German manufacturing orders fell by a sharper than expected 3.2 percent month-on-month in June. \par \par \uc2  Headline German unemployment also vaulted the politically-sensitive four million mark on an unadjusted basis in July, hitting German Chancellor Gerhard Schroeder's re-election chances six weeks ahead of polling day. \par \par \uc2  European financial market players want conservative Edmund Stoiber to win the September election and expect the euro to strengthen and German share prices to rise if he does, according to a Reuters poll released on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  U.S. July import and export prices for July are due at 1230 GMT. Import prices are forecast to have risen by 0.2 percent, after falling 0.6 percent in June. \par \par \uc2  FLAGGING GROWTH \par \par \uc2  The International Monetary Fund has slashed growth forecasts for the world's leading economies, a German newspaper said in its Wednesday edition. \par \par \uc2  The Boersen Zeitung said that according to internal forecasts it had seen, the IMF now predicts the U.S. economy will grow by 2.2 percent this year, compared with its public forecast of 2.5 percent. \par \par \uc2  Japan spent a record amount of 4.0162 trillion yen on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  between April and June, \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  data showed on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on seven days between May 22 and June 28, selling the yen and buying dollars and euros. \par \par \uc2  Japanese authorities were seeking to head off a potentially export-damaging rise in the yen. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020807dy8700o3d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
