\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar rides high on U.S. stocks, rate cut talk. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Carolyn Cohn \par \uc2 579 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 August 2002\par 12:27\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, Aug 7 (Reuters) - The dollar held up near recent six-week peaks against the yen and the euro on Wednesday on increasing expectations of an asset-boosting U.S. rate cut and on talk of U.S. funds bringing money home. \par \par \uc2  U.S. blue-chip stocks rose by nearly three percent on Tuesday on mounting speculation that the Fed would trim rates by the end of the year. Such a move would boost the U.S. economy and U.S. stocks, and therefore the dollar, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  Analysts also said some funds were buying U.S. shares to maintain the balance of their asset allocations after the value of U.S. stock portfolios declined sharply in recent months. \par \par \uc2  "We've had a such a significant rally on Wall Street that dollar strength is not really surprising," said Ryan Shea, senior international economist at Bank One. \par \par \uc2  "There's a lot of speculation that the Fed will cut interest rates - 25 basis points may not do a lot, but it's helping sentiment towards the dollar." \par \par \uc2  The dollar was trading at 120.80/85 yen and $0.9672/74 per euro by 0950 GMT, little changed from the U.S. close but slightly below six-week highs of 121.21 yen and $0.9619 per euro hit on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The euro brushed off data showing German manufacturing orders fell by a sharper than expected 3.2 percent month-on-month in June. \par \par \uc2  Headline German unemployment also vaulted the politically-sensitive four million mark on an unadjusted basis in July, hitting German Chancellor Gerhard Schroeder's re-election chances six weeks ahead of polling day. \par \par \uc2  European financial market players want conservative Edmund Stoiber to win the September election and expect the euro to strengthen and German share prices to rise if he does, according to a Reuters poll released on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  DUMPING BONDS \par \par \uc2  Dealers said some investors were seen to have sold a huge amount of two-year Schatz debt and shifted funds to European and U.S stocks. On Tuesday, the Schatz yield rose by a hefty 12 basis points. \par \par \uc2  Traders also said hedge funds were dumping short-term government bonds to buy stocks. \par \par \uc2  "U.S. assets are quite cheap, and that's when people start picking them up," said David Bloom, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at HSBC Markets. \par \par \uc2  U.S. stock index futures were indicating a stronger opening on Wall Street, after networking giant Cisco Systems posted higher quarterly earnings in after-hours trade. \par \par \uc2  But market bears remained sceptical about the dollar's outlook, saying there was a risk of a U.S. double-dip recession despite official talk that the U.S. economy was sound. \par \par \uc2  The International Monetary Fund has slashed growth forecasts for the world's leading economies, a German newspaper said in its Wednesday edition. \par \par \uc2  The Boersen Zeitung said that according to internal forecasts it had seen, the IMF now predicts the U.S. economy will grow by 2.2 percent this year, compared with its public forecast of 2.5 percent. \par \par \uc2  Japan spent a record amount of 4.0162 trillion yen on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  between April and June, \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  data showed on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on seven days between May 22 and June 28, selling the yen and buying dollars and euros. \par \par \uc2  Japanese authorities were seeking to head off a potentially export-damaging rise in the yen. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020807dy8700kuj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
