\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Japan interventions \highlight\uc2  at Y4.0162 trln in April-June. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Chikafumi Hodo \par \uc2 930 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 August 2002\par 11:23\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Aug 7 (Reuters) - Concerned that a stronger yen would derail an export-led economic recovery, \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  spent a record-high amount on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  between April and June. \par \par \uc2  The authorities forked out 4.0162 trillion yen ($33.20 billion) on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sap the yen's strength during the three-month period, \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MOF) data showed on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ), which acts as an agent for the ministry, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on seven days between May 22 and June 28, selling the yen and buying dollars and euros. \par \par \uc2  It was the largest quarterly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  figure since the ministry started disclosing such data in 1991. \par \par \uc2  During the quarter, the BOJ was first seen stepping into the market on May 22 to buy dollars at around 123.80 yen, a level regarded as one of the highest ever at which the BOJ has conducted dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  At 0303 GMT, the dollar was quoted at 120.92/97 yen. \par \par \uc2  The authorities have kept out of the market since June 28, even when the dollar dropped to a 17-month low of 115.50 yen on July 16, and their silence has confused many participants. \par \par \uc2  "The amount was enough to absorb the demand to sell dollars to cover Japan's massive current account surplus, as well as speculative selling during the period," said Takashi Toyahara, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  section manager at Nomura Securities. \par \par \uc2  "Speculators could buy back the dollar further if its recent recovery proves to be firm, but there is still strong downside risk," Toyahara said. \par \par \uc2  MINISTRY SOUNDING OUT INVESTORS \par \par \uc2  The authorities may be facing a moment of truth in deciding the timing of any further dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , given the fragility of the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  due to growing concerns over a possible U.S. economic slump stemming from weak share prices. \par \par \uc2  Despite the dollar's recovery to a six-week high of 121.23 yen in offshore trade on Tuesday, the ministry could be worried about the greenback's outlook after the previous \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  failed to put an immediate halt to the yen's uptrend. \par \par \uc2  Given its experience in May and June, the ministry could be studying ways to make future \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  more effective, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  In recent weeks, it has individually invited senior fund managers from banks and institutions, including life insurers, asking for information such as portfolio breakdowns and specific details on when investors act in the market. \par \par \uc2  There were mixed views on the intention of the meetings, with several participating managers saying they got the impression that the ministry was looking at timings for future \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  It was not unusual for investors to meet with the ministry, which in the past was said to have tried to influence them by telling them when to buy or sell dollars. \par \par \uc2  "In the previous \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  (in May and June), we got the impression that the MOF had ignored domestic institutional investors and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily," one fund manager said. \par \par \uc2  "But the MOF now may be trying to take a different approach. Maybe they were trying to seek support from institutional investors should the MOF actually \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he said. \par \par \uc2  NEXT \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  Japanese investors are expected to have a tough time at their interim bookclosings in September, with the yen's firmness reducing values of foreign-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  denominated assets and the slump in domestic share prices also likely to hurt earnings. \par \par \uc2  Japan struggled out of recession in the first quarter of this year after three quarters of contraction. \par \par \uc2  With domestic demand still sluggish, manufacturers have fueled the recovery and the authorities are concerned that a stronger yen will choke off growth in exports. \par \par \uc2  As Japan's hands are effectively tied on fiscal and monetary policy, a weak yen is considered to be one of the few weapons left to help the economy. \par \par \uc2  "A weak yen clearly had a positive impact toward helping the economy both on the micro and macro sides at the end of March, so the MOF should continue to keep the yen weak," said Michihisa Tanimoto, deputy general manager at Sumitomo Life Insurance. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  played an important role in assisting share prices and boosting the economy so it is important to keep the yen weak," he said. \par \par \uc2  Tanimoto said the success of future \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  depends on whether the Japanese government can present its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy clearly to the market. \par \par \uc2  But many players disagree that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would work effectively now when pessimism toward the U.S. economy is growing and concerns over the dollar's fall are intensifying. "Many domestic investors dream about the (dollar) rally seen in 1995, but the trend is totally different from that time when joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  worked effectively because the U.S. economy was still booming at that time," the fund manager said. \par \par \uc2  "Should \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the present time, even with help from the United States, I think the move would fall victim to hedge funds, who surely would dump dollars on rallies," he said. \par \par \uc2  Following is a table of net \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  amounts during the April-June quarter in billions of yen. \par \par \uc2   date   total amount    \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pairs \par \par \uc2   May  22    587.1     dollar buying/yen selling \par \par \uc2   May  23    499.1     dollar buying/yen selling \par \par \uc2   May  31  1,031.2     dollar buying/yen selling \par \par \uc2   June  4    372.7     dollar buying/yen selling \par \par \uc2   June 24    429.0     dollar buying/yen selling \par \par \uc2   June 26    568.7     dollar buying/yen selling \par \par \uc2   June 28    504.6     dollar buying/yen selling \par \par \uc2   June 28     23.8     euro buying/yen selling \par \par \uc2   ($1=120.95 yen). \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020807dy8700ium\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
