\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  June 28 dlr-buy  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  worth Y520.5 bln. \b0\par\par\uc2 257 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Juli 2002\par 12:29\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, July 31 (Reuters) - The Japanese monetary authorities spent about 520.5 billion yen in buying dollars in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on June 28, according to Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOJ) data on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The BOJ data showed that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MOF) paid that amount, which according to dealers translates into about $4.37 billion, to the private sector through its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  account, which mostly represents \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. \par \par \uc2  On June 28, the BOJ, which acts as the agent of the MOF, was seen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  when the dollar hit a low of around 118.36 yen in overseas trade, sending it as high as 120.15 yen that day, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The MOF has confirmed that the BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  that day, but it does not reveal which \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  it buys and sells or at which levels. \par \par \uc2  Looking at the moves that day, dealers said the average dollar level would be around 119 yen, giving the $4.37 billion calculation. \par \par \uc2  Concerned that a stronger yen would derail an export-led economic recovery, \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on seven occasion between May 22 and June 28, but the authorities have kept out of the market since then. \par \par \uc2  On July 16, the dollar dropped to a 17-month low of 115.50 yen, but it climbed back to a nearly four-week high of 120.42 yen in Tokyo morning trade on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  As of 1023 GMT, the dollar was quoted at 120.01/06 yen . \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020731dy7v00kpd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
