\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Yen falls as  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  raises fear of  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2  By Javier David \par \uc2 875 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Juli 2002\par 16:02\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  (Updates with U.S. open, adds quotes, changes dateline, previous LONDON) \par \par \uc2  NEW YORK, July 22 (Reuters) - The yen fell from last week's 17-month high against the dollar and dipped against the euro on Monday after warnings from Japanese officials prompted speculation that authorities may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the yen. \par \par \uc2  In Asia, Japanese Finance Minister Masajuro Shiokawa said \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  stood ready to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets at any time to counter excessive volatility and to dampen the effect a strong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has on the country's export-led recovery. \par \par \uc2  "It goes without saying that a weaker yen would be desirable from the standpoint of trade balances," the finance minister said. "We are thus paying due attention to market developments and stand ready to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  at any time if there are extreme movements." \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , however, has seen its efforts to suppress the yen's advance frustrated by a broad-based decline in the value of the dollar, exacerbated by steep losses in U.S. stocks that have sent major indexes hurtling to multiyear lows. \par \par \uc2  "In some form or another there will be some significant dollar buying (by the Japanese)," said Michael McGuinness, head of North American sales at American Express Bank. "The Japanese have made comments about how 115 yen was an important level ... and I don't think we'll breach it." \par \par \uc2  Japanese monetary authorities sold the yen on several occasions during May and June, but have kept their powder dry recently as the market contends with overwhelming bearishness on U.S. assets and the dollar. \par \par \uc2  In early U.S. trading, the dollar bought 116.40 yen, up nearly half a percent from its prior closing level and above its weakest level since February 2001, set just last week. \par \par \uc2  The euro traded at session lows near 1.0075 , as the Dow Jones industrial average and the Nasdaq Composite shook off early weakness and traded slightly higher despite telecommunications giant WorldCom Inc.'s filing for bankruptcy. \par \par \uc2  Against the yen, the euro changed hands above 117.30 yen , up 0.15 percent on the day. \par \par \uc2  IMM floor traders said flows were light at the start of pit trade, with dealers awaiting the open of U.S. equity markets. \par \par \uc2  "Everyone's program reads that the stock market has to get through the first hour and see if it recovers from Friday's overload selling," said one floor trader. \par \par \uc2  September euros were in a tight range off a two-session low of $1.0042. September yen also were lower but confined to an inside range of $0.008590 to $0.008679. \par \par \uc2  STOCKS, STOCKS, STOCKS \par \par \uc2  Dealers said investors had already bet heavily against the dollar on concerns about U.S. accounting practices and stocks recently, leaving little scope for further selling at the moment and so had elected to take profits on the euro's sharp gains. The Dow plunged 4.64 percent on Friday, its seventh-largest point decline ever. \par \par \uc2  "People are short already and we know about the stock market already," said Rob Hayward, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at ABN-Amro. "There's also some realization that equity weakness will also hit Europe." \par \par \uc2  Telecom giant WorldCom Inc. filed the largest U.S. bankruptcy ever on Sunday after the company buckled under the weight of a $3.85 billion accounting scandal and a mountain of junk-rated debt. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  WARINESS \par \par \uc2  In addition to Finance Minister Shiokawa's remarks, Vice Finance Minister Toshiro Muto said Japan was prepared to communicate with overseas authorities on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  matters. \par \par \uc2  Senior Japanese Finance Ministry official Zembei Mizoguchi said he was carefully watching the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, and he believed the fundamentals of the U.S. economy were strong. \par \par \uc2  The Swiss National Bank lowered its repo rate two basis points to 0.93 percent earlier. The Swiss franc was largely unchanged on the move, trading at 1.4445 against the dollar and 1.4555 versus the euro. The SNB has been tweaking its repo rates in the past few months as it has been concerned about the strength of the franc. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bid prices at 1347GMT. All data taken from Reuters \par \par \uc2  calculated from the levels at 5:30 p.m. (21:30 GMT) in the \par \par \uc2  previous New York session. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Last  US Close    %      YTD     2001\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 19 July  Change %Change    Close\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -------------------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Euro/dlr             1.0072   1.0113   -0.41  +13.12   0.8904\par Dlr/yen              116.44   115.85   +0.51  -11.54   131.63\par Euro/yen             117.23   117.17   +0.05   -0.01   117.24\par Dlr/swiss            1.4451   1.4420   +0.21  -12.91   1.6594\par Stg/dlr              1.5742   1.5765   -0.15   +8.26   1.4541\par Dlr/cad              1.5503   1.5430   +0.47   -2.60   1.5917\par Aus/dlr              0.5516   0.5565   -0.88   +8.03   0.5106\par Euro/swiss           1.4