\par\par \b \uc2  ANALYSIS-Greenspan  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  remarks seen upping  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  bets. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Carolyn Cohn \par \uc2 750 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Juli 2002\par 14:45\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, July 17 (Reuters) - The possibility of coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to halt the dollar's slide has flickered onto traders' radar screens, following comments from the U.S. Federal Reserve Chairman and from Japan. \par \par \uc2  The dollar has fallen by more than 13 percent against the yen and the euro since April, taking its cue from battered U.S. stocks. \par \par \uc2  Repeated solo \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Japanese authorities to sell yen and so protect \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's budding export-led recovery have failed to head off the dollar decline. \par \par \uc2  Fed Chairman Alan Greenspan made rare comments about the dollar in his testimony to the Senate panel on Tuesday, and this could be the first signal that the United States is unwilling to let the dollar fall indefinitely, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  "\b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  is certainly looking more likely and coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  can't be ruled out," said Neil MacKinnon at the ECU Group in London. \par \par \uc2  "Coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  may be the only way of breaking the vicious spiral of a weaker dollar leading to weaker stocks." WHAT DID HE MEAN? \par \par \uc2  In his testimony, Greenspan threw up a "flag of caution" about forecasts of a much weaker dollar, saying exchange rates were "extraordinarily difficult" to predict. \par \par \uc2  "Greenspan was not just warning about the profession of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  forecasting but more importantly arguing that the market should not expect the dollar to decline continuously," said Shahab Jalinoos, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at UBS Warburg, in a client note. \par \par \uc2  "The Fed Chairman may have been implicitly saying that the U.S. authorities will not tolerate indefinite \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakness...Though the prospect of coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to slow the fall of the dollar is clearly still low, we note that the market should start to price in such risks more significantly going forward." \par \par \uc2  Japanese policy-makers were quick to capitalise on the remarks, raising the spectre of coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's top government spokesman Yasuo Fukuda said on Wednesday the Japanese authorities could coordinate with their U.S. counterparts on \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the need arose. \par \par \uc2  Shortly afterwards, Japanese Finance Minister Masajuro Shiokawa said Japan's top financial diplomat, Haruhiko Kuroda, was keeping in touch with his overseas counterparts on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 JAPAN\b0 \highlight\uc2  GOING SOLO \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell yen on at least seven days in May and June, spending an estimated $30 billion of yen. Exporters benefit from a weaker \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as it reduces the prices of their goods. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  last \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on June 28, enlisting the help of the U.S. Federal Reserve and the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but only as intermediaries for its yen sales. The U.S. and euro zone central banks did not spend any of their own money. \par \par \uc2  Since then, the dollar has fallen by 3.5 percent against the yen, hitting 17-month lows below 115.50 on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The dollar has also plunged through the psychologically key one-for-one level with the euro this week, extending its losses by Wednesday to 2-1/2 year lows beyond $1.0150 . \par \par \uc2  The speed of the move may alarm the United States, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  "They (U.S. authorities) want to ensure the dollar doesn't become a one-way bet," said Derek Halpenny, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  economist at Bank of Tokyo-Mitsubishi. \par \par \uc2  "If we can stabilise and consolidate at levels of parity up to $1.05, I doubt the administration would be that concerned. But if we were to see a rapid move beyond there to $1.10 as quickly as we've come from $0.90, that would be a concern." \par \par \uc2  U.S. MAY CRY OFF \par \par \uc2  Previous comments from U.S. policy-makers have indicated the Bush administration is reluctant to take on the markets and dictate the dollar's direction. \par \par \uc2  Some analysts remain unconvinced, therefore, that the latest remarks from Greenspan and Japanese ministers herald a sea-change. \par \par \uc2  "\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  may invite the U.S. to the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  party but I'm not sure they would come," said Steven Englander, global \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Citibank. \par \par \uc2  "I don't think the U.S. has any interest in being seen to manipulate its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." \par \par \uc2  Hans Redeker, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at BNP Paribas, also said he did not expect to see coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but added that current market conditions suggested it would be a good time for the Japanese authorities to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "Our research of yen market positions shows that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  now would be more successful than at the end of June - the Bank of Japan could come in again very soon." \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020717dy7h00p0q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
