\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar pulls off lows as US stock futures gain. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Charlotte Cooper \par \uc2 698 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Juli 2002\par 10:37\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, July 17 (Reuters) - The dollar pulled back from a two-year low against the euro and a three-year low on the Swiss franc on Wednesday as U.S. stock futures turned higher, stopping dollar bears in their tracks. \par \par \uc2  The dollar has been held hostage to the fortunes of U.S. stocks in recent weeks, as worries over earnings and question marks over corporate governance have battered investor confidence in U.S. assets. \par \par \uc2  A timely reminder from a Japanese government official that Tokyo could coordinate with U.S. counterparts on \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  if need be added impetus to the bounce, helping to propel the dollar nearly a yen up from a recent 17-month low. \par \par \uc2  "U.S. stock futures are now up which is helping the dollar, but the market is very volatile," said Steven Englander, global \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Citibank. \par \par \uc2  "\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  may invite the U.S to the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  party but I'm not sure they would come. I don't think the U.S. has any interest in being seen to manipulate its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Worried about the yen's rise, the Japanese authorities have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market at least seven times over the past two months but they have stayed out of the market over the past two weeks as the dollar has fallen rapidly. \par \par \uc2  By 0827 GMT the dollar was trading at 116.25 yen, up nearly a yen from 17-month lows set on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The euro, which earlier scaled fresh highs at $1.0162, pulled back in choppy trade to $1.0095, down slightly on the day. The Swiss franc was at 1.4525 per dollar, after peaking at 1.4443 earlier. \par \par \uc2  U.S. EARNINGS WATCH \par \par \uc2  Traders were looking ahead to earnings for several key U.S. companies including Citigroup, JP Morgan Chase and IBM, after Wall Street fell on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  A relatively upbeat testimony on the economy from Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan on Tuesday failed to lift market pessimism after a slew of corporate accounting scandals that have damaged investor confidence in U.S. assets. \par \par \uc2  "The markets chose to focus on the negative aspects of Greenspan's speech, like worries about corporate responsibility, the risk of domestic terrorism and the fact that the consumer is not going to sustain the U.S. economy for ever," said Shahab Jalinoos, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at UBS Warburg. \par \par \uc2  Greenspan speaks again on Wednesday this time to the House of Representatives Financial Services Committee but is not expected to deviate from his speech on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  WORDS BUT NO ACTION \par \par \uc2  Japan's Chief Cabinet Secretary Yasuo Fukuda joined a chorus of Tokyo officials bemoaning the yen's export-choking rise, saying Japanese authorities could coordinate with their U.S. counterparts on \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the need arose. \par \par \uc2  Earlier senior Finance Ministry official Zembei Mizoguchi said the dollar's weakness was unlikely to be long lasting, given the strength of the U.S. economy, according to Japan's Jiji news agency. \par \par \uc2  Mizoguchi, the head of the ministry's international bureau, also reiterated that Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy was unchanged - that it would take necessary action when needed. \par \par \uc2  However the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 's agent for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , has been conspicuous by its absence in the last couple of weeks, even as the dollar has fallen to fresh lows. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on seven occasions between May 22 and June 28 and is estimated to have bought a total of about $30 billion in \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "In this mood, the dollar is likely to fall below the key support of 115 yen and once the level is broken, many would forecast it to drop towards 110 yen," said Michihisa Tanimoto, deputy general manager at Sumitomo Life Insurance. \par \par \uc2  "Japan could step in at any time, but I feel the key to the success of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  depends on whether the monetary authorities can present their \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy clearly to the market," Tanimoto said. \par \par \uc2  In the euro zone, industrial production is expected to have fallen by 0.1 percent in May after a 0.5 percent fall in April. The figures are due at 1000 GMT. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020717dy7h00hwk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
