\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar recovers slightly on  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  jitters. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Chikafumi Hodo \par \uc2 878 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Juli 2002\par 06:25\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, July 17 (Reuters) - The dollar edged up against the yen in Tokyo morning trade on Wednesday on bargain-hunting from Japanese pension funds and lingering wariness about Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which encouraged light short-covering. \par \par \uc2  Some U.S. operators were also rumoured to be shifting their funds from overseas instruments back into dollars, either because they did not want to take \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  risks or because they had taken profits overseas to cover U.S. equity losses, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "It was about time we saw some short-covering, but I think this is a very healthy correction, which we witnessed several times before the dollar came under selling pressure in the current phase," a Japanese securities firm dealer said. \par \par \uc2  "The dollar's undertone remains bearish as the market still continues to be concerned about U.S. accounting problems and falling share prices," the dealer added. \par \par \uc2  The dollar rose to a session high of 116.30 yen on bids from pension funds and Japanese retail investors in particular. Individuals were showing interest in putting their summer bonuses into foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bonds, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  But offers were rumoured to be lined up around 116.50 yen, with major sell orders said to be placed above 117 yen. \par \par \uc2  As of 0255 GMT, the dollar was quoted at 116.01/06 yen against 115.63/73 yen in late U.S. trade on Tuesday. The dollar fell to a fresh 17-month low of 115.50 yen overnight. \par \par \uc2  The euro was at $1.0108/18 against $1.0115/20 in late U.S. trade. It rose to a fresh 2-= year high of $1.0148 on Tuesday, with many dealers forecasting the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  would test $1.02 in the near term. \par \par \uc2  The euro was firm at 117.27/36 yen against 117.04 yen in late U.S. trade. \par \par \uc2  Many profit-takers and exporters were rumoured to be placing heavy offers between 117.50 and 118.00 yen. \par \par \uc2  GREENSPAN OFFERS LITTLE HELP \par \par \uc2  Despite the recovery on Wednesday morning, the dollar was still frail after seven straight sessions of decline in the U.S. blue chip Dow Jones industrial average. \par \par \uc2  Tuesday's closely watched Congressional testimony by Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan failed to help sentiment in U.S. asset markets, or in the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Greenspan gave an upbeat message, saying the U.S. economy was resilient and improving but needed time to heal after a barrage of corporate scandals. \par \par \uc2  Stepping into an area normally under the purview of the U.S. Treasury Secretary, Greenspan also made reference to the dollar, offering a "flag of caution" regarding forecasts of a further decline in the dollar. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 JAPAN\b0 \highlight\uc2 'S \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  Dollar bears took a cautious attitude, with wariness about Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  stronger in Tokyo than in other key financial centres, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Senior Finance Ministry official Zembei Mizoguchi said the dollar's weakness was unlikely to be long-lasting, given the strength of the U.S. economy, Jiji news agency reported. \par \par \uc2  Mizoguchi, the head of the ministry's international bureau, was quoted by Jiji as saying that Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy was unchanged - that it would take necessary action when needed. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on seven occasions between May 22 and June 28 and is estimated to have bought a total of about $30 billion in \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but the Japanese authorities have kept out of the market for two weeks despite the dollar's fall. \par \par \uc2  "In this mood, the dollar is likely to fall below the key support of 115 yen and once the level is broken, many would forecast it to drop towards 110 yen," said Michihisa Tanimoto, deputy general manager at Sumitomo Life Insurance. \par \par \uc2  "Japan could step in at any time, but I feel the key to the success of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  fully depends on whether the monetary authorities can present their \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy clearly to the market," Tanimoto said. \par \par \uc2  "I think at the moment the market is not getting a clear message why \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The authorities are failing to communicate with the market," Tanimoto said. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bids prices at 0314 GMT. All data taken from Reuters with percent change calculated from the daily U.S. close at 2130 GMT. \par \par \uc2   Last     US Close  % Chg  YTD %   2001 Cls \par \par \uc2   16 Jul. \par \par \uc2   ---------------------------------------- \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Euro/dlr       1.0109   1.0115   -0.06    +6.46   0.9496\par  Dlr/yen        115.96   115.83   +0.11    +1.32   114.45\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Euro/yen    117.25   117.16   +0.08    +7.86   108.71\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Dlr/swiss      1.4500   1.4492   +0.06    -9.44   1.6012\par  Stg/dlr        1.5740   1.5751   -0.07    +4.93   1.5000\par  Can/dlr        1.5380   1.5375   +0.03    +3.12   1.4914\par  Aus/dlr        0.5572   0.5570   +0.04    -0