\par\par \b \uc2  Following are some of the main Asian business news stories... \b0\par\par\uc2 866 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Juli 2002\par 07:21\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  Following are some of the main Asian business news stories (all times GMT) \par \par \uc2  - - - - \par \par \uc2  MARKETS \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE - Asian shares find no impetus from a late Wall Street turnaround and head lower after a cautious start, while the euro keeps its head above dollar parity as global markets steel for testimony from U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief Alan Greenspan. \par \par \uc2  (MARKETS-GLOBAL (WRAPUP 2) BY CHRISTOPHER KAUFMAN, EXPECT BY 0730) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO - \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers question the Japanese authorities' determination to stem the yen's rise, puzzled that, after strong \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  earlier, Tokyo has stayed out of the market for over two weeks despite the dollar's tumble to 17-month lows. \par \par \uc2  (MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 JAPAN\b0 \highlight\uc2 -\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2 , BY CHIKAFUMI HODO, EXPECT BY 0730) \par \par \uc2  (SEE ALSO MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1), BY HIDEYUKI SANO, EXPECT BY 0700) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG - The crony capitalism, vested family interests and market immaturity that have dogged Asian asset markets are now protecting regional equities from the fallout of crumbling consumer confidence and corporate scandals that have sent U.S. stocks to five year lows, analysts say. \par \par \uc2  (FINANCIAL-ASIA-SCANDALS (ANALYSIS), BY NICK EDWARDS, EXPECT BY 0900) \par \par \uc2  - - - - \par \par \uc2  ECONOMY \par \par \uc2  TOKYO - Corporate Japan gets a reality check as the yen reaches breakeven point for many of the big exporters that helped pull Japan out of recession this year; electronics giants Pioneer and Matsushita the latest to clamour for a return to weak yen. \par \par \uc2  (ECONOMY-JAPAN-COMPANIES, BY JASON SZEP, EXPECT BY 0800) \par \par \uc2  (SEE ALSO ECONOMY-JAPAN (UPDATE 2), BY SHINICHI KISHIMA, MOVED) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG - Hong Kong is expected to report its jobless rate edged up to 7.6 percent in the three months to June, a record, and economists say things will only get worse in months ahead. \par \par \uc2  (ECONOMY-HONGKONG-JOBS (UPDATE 1), BY TAY HAN NEE, EXPECT BY 0900) \par \par \uc2  (SEE ALSO ECONOMY-HONGKONG-JOBS-PEOPLE, BY TAN EE LYN, EXPECT BY 0900, PICTURE) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE - Singapore's non-oil exports are expected to have risen modestly in June as the trade-driven city state sputters out of recession with electronics shipments still weak. \par \par \uc2  (ECONOMY-SINGAPORE-TRADE (UPDATE 1), BY JACQUELINE WONG, EXPECT BY 0800) \par \par \uc2  SEOUL - The South Korean won's rise to fresh 20-month highs drew a warning of sustained strength from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday and a swift response by the Finance Ministry to play down the comments. \par \par \uc2  (ECONOMY-KOREA-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1) BY LEE SUJUNG, MOVED) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO - Botswana might seem an unlikely benchmark for Asia's big economies. But in tracing the roots of China's phenomenal growth, a U.S. academic finds parallels with the way institutions developed in the fast-growing southern African country, which now enjoys a higher sovereign credit rating than Japan. \par \par \uc2  (ECONOMY-ASIA-BOTSWANA, BY ALAN WHEATLEY, EXPECT BY 0830) \par \par \uc2  - - - - \par \par \uc2  IPOS \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG - Shares of tycoon Li Ka-shing's biotech spinoff CK Life Sciences, among the most heavily hyped Hong Kong IPOs in years, climb nearly nine percent in their trading debut but the performance is a far cry from the stellar gains of the multibillionaire's last offering, Internet portal tom.com. \par \par \uc2  (HEALTH-CKLIFE (UPDATE 3), BY BEI BEI SHE AND AZHAR SUKRI, EXPECT BY 0800) \par \par \uc2  HONG KONG - Despite bad loan fears, Bank of China Hong Kong's IPO is proving popular with retail punters hungry for returns but with few compelling options during a time of low interest rates, a weak stock market and depressed property prices. \par \par \uc2  (FINANCIAL-HONGKONG-BANKOFCHINA (ANALYSIS), BY DOMINIC LAU, EXPECT BY 0900) \par \par \uc2  - - - - \par \par \uc2  TELECOMS \par \par \uc2  TOKYO - In Japan, where consumers often choose cellphones over PCs to access the Internet, handset makers have led the way with pioneering work on full-colour screens and wireless Web-surfing; miniature cameras are the latest development and photo-phone shipments are expected to nearly quadruple this year. \par \par \uc2  (TELECOMS-JAPAN-CAMERAPHONES (ANALYSIS), BY ERIKO AMAHA, EXPECT BY 0730) \par \par \uc2  SEOUL - SK Telecom Co, South Korea's biggest mobile phone operator, agreed on Tuesday to sell 340.3 billion won ($293 million) in KT Corp exchangeable bonds to four financial institutions. \par \par \uc2  (TELECOM-KOREA-SKT (UPDATE 2), BY JUDY LEE, EXPECT BY 0700) \par \par \uc2  - - - - \par \par \uc2  CORPORATE \par \par \uc2  BANGKOK - The president of Thailand's biggest industrial conglomerate, Siam Cement Plc, speaks to Reuters in an interview about the outlook for the company following a radical corporate restructuring. \par \par \uc2  (CONSTRUCTION-THAILAND-SIAM (UPDATE 1), BY ANDREW MARSHALL, EXPECT BY 0800) \par \par \uc2  SYDNEY - Shares in Australian miner WMC Ltd plunge to a 10-month low after it warns that smelter repair work at its giant outback copper mine will lower production and cut earnings. (MINERALS-AUSTRALIA-WMC (UPDATE 4), BY JAMES REGAN, EXPECT BY 0700) \par \par \uc2  - - - - \par \par \uc2  TRANSPORT \par \par \uc2  SHENZHEN, China - Driven by China's sizzling export growth, container traffic in the booming southern port of Shenzhen is expected to rise by 20 percent this year, exceeding previous forecasts and biting a bit further into Hong Kong's share of the prosperous cargo trade in the Pearl River Delta. \par \par \uc2  (TRANSPORT-HONGKONG-SHENZHEN, MOVED) \par \par \uc2  (SEE ALSO TRANSPORT-HONGKONG-CHINA (ANALYSIS), EXPECT BY 0930; TRANSPORT-CHINA-CHIWAN (INTERVIEW), BY ALISON LEUNG, EXPECT BY 0930; AND TRANSPORT-CHINA-SHENZHENPORT-TABLE, EXPECT BY 0930) \par \par \uc2  - - - - \par \par \uc2  If you have any queries, please call: \par \par \uc2  Singapore (65) 870-3818 \par \par \uc2  Comments to: asia.newseds@reuters.com. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020716dy7g00fgf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
