\par\par \b \uc2  Dollar sinks to post-Sept. 11 low vs. yen. \b0\par\par\uc2 190 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Juli 2002\par 16:11\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NEW YORK, July 15 (Reuters) - The dollar slumped to a post-Sept. 11 low against the yen on Monday, heightening market concerns about \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to rein in the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The greenback, under broad pressure after hitting parity with the euro earlier in the session, traded as low as 115.65 yen, its weakest level since February 2001. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the dollar's break below the prior post-Sept. 11 low of 115.76 yen raised the risk that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  will launch a new yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market. \par \par \uc2  Japanese Finance Minister Masajuro Shiokawa said on Sunday that it would be problematic if the dollar fell to around 115 yen, adding that since Washington supported a "strong dollar" policy, it should make efforts to stabilize stock prices and show that its economy was strong. He added that a dollar value in the range of 125 to 135 yen would be good for the Japanese economy. \par \par \uc2  Japanese monetary authorities, concerned that yen strength will hurt the export-led economy, have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets seven times since late May. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020715dy7f00rsp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
