\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dlr near 10-month lows vs yen, awaits U.S. data. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Sumeet Desai \par \uc2 512 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Juli 2002\par 12:09\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, July 12 (Reuters) - The dollar hovered near the previous day's 10-month lows against the yen on Friday as comments from Japanese Finance Minister Masajuro Shiokawa left the impression that yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was not imminent. \par \par \uc2  Shiokawa told a news conference that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  would act against excessive volatility in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, but that the dollar's decline against the yen seemed to be less rapid than two weeks earlier. \par \par \uc2  Concern about the performance of U.S. assets has hit the dollar in recent months, but the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has found some support from the threat of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , following Japanese action on at least seven days since late May. \par \par \uc2  "Shiokawa said the rate of decline is not as much as it was but to be honest that is not the case at all," said Ryan Shea, senior international economist at BankOne. \par \par \uc2  "He may be trying to play down \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  expectations." \par \par \uc2  The dollar was at 116.79/84 yen at 0955 GMT, around 0.20 percent down from late New York trade, and from Thursday's low of 116.41. \par \par \uc2  The euro was trading at $0.9890/93, little changed from late U.S. trade after a recovery in U.S. stocks pushed the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  off its highs around $0.9940. \par \par \uc2  The Nasdaq index closed 2.11 percent higher on Thursday, following heavy losses in the previous session, and Nasdaq futures were trading strongly in European trade. \par \par \uc2  DATA WATCH \par \par \uc2  Dealers said focus would remain on U.S. retail sales data due at 1230 GMT and consumer sentiment figures at 1345 GMT later in the session and the likely effect on U.S. stock markets. \par \par \uc2  Economists polled by Reuters on average expect sales to rise 0.7 percent overall and 0.5 percent excluding autos, erasing most of the previous month's losses. \par \par \uc2  The preliminary University of Michigan consumer sentiment index for July is expected to rise to 92.8 from the previous 92.4. \par \par \uc2  "The data will be key. I think people will be happier to sell the dollar on a weak number than buy on a strong number," said Adrian Schmidt, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at RBS Financial Markets. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said overall sentiment on the dollar remained very negative as the greenback continues to be dogged by concerns about U.S. corporate accounting practices and doubts about the U.S. recovery. \par \par \uc2  The dollar, which has lost more than 10 percent against both the euro and the yen so far this year, has even come within spitting distance of parity with the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the last few weeks. \par \par \uc2  Euro zone finance ministers and representatives of the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and European Commission issued a rare joint statement on Thursday, welcoming the euro's rise. \par \par \uc2  European Union finance ministers are meeting on Friday in Brussels. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said that with the trend for a weaker dollar intact, further Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was almost a certainty. \par \par \uc2  "To be honest, the BOJ has to come in again," said Shea. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020712dy7c00jsm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
