\par\par \b \uc2  Osaka Shares End Down On Broad-Based Selling; Hurt By  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 306 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Juli 2002\par 09:09\par \uc2  Dow Jones Asian Equities Report \par \uc2 AER\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (Nikkei/Dow Jones)--Stocks traded on the Osaka Securities Exchange ended lower Thursday following big losses on Wall Street, and as a weaker dollar exacerbated the market's negative mood, market participants said. \par \par \uc2  The OSE adjusted average for the first section finished down 353.50 points, or 2.1%, at 16477.77 for a second straight day of losses. \par \par \uc2  Export-heavy technology issues were hard hit by the dollar's weakness against the yen, which erodes the price competitiveness of Japanese products abroad and deflates overseas earnings when repatriated. \par \par \uc2  The dollar slid as low as Y117.51, but clawed back most of its losses to reach the high-Y117s, where it stayed well-supported on fears \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  might \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell yen. \par \par \uc2  Amid a dearth on fresh trading cues in the stock market, selling was broad-based and included domestic-demand issues, such as pharmaceuticals and housing stocks, which tend to get a boost when technology stocks are shunned. \par \par \uc2  Decliners outnumbered advancers by a wide margin of 74 to 25, while 18 issues ended flat. \par \par \uc2  Among decliners were Ono Pharmaceutical, down 2.4% at Y4,450 on profit-taking by investors wary of recent top-heaviness; export-heavy Murata Manufacturing, off 2.6% at Y7,220; and technology heavyweight Nidec, down 3.2% at Y8,430. \par \par \uc2  Gainers included mail-order company Simree, up 5.0% at Y740 on bargain-hunting, and women's apparel maker King, up 1.2% at Y175 after showing resilience near the Y170 threshold. \par \par \uc2  General contractor Matsumura-Gumi was up 1.8% at Y58. Prices below Y100 are often viewed as signaling financial difficulties. \par \par \uc2  Overnight, the Dow Jones Industrial Average sank 3.1% to 8813.50. The Nasdaq Composite Index dropped 2.5% to 1346.02. \par \par \uc2 Dokument aer0000020020711dy7b00335\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw200\pich25\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3000\pichgoal375
