\par\par \b \uc2  MOF Shiokawa Quoted: Will  \highlight22\uc2 Intervene \highlight\uc2  In  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  As Needed \b0\par\par\uc2 222 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Juli 2002\par 11:57\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO -(Dow Jones)- \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets as needed, Finance Minister Masajuro Shiokawa told a meeting of economic ministers and senior ruling coalition members Thursday, a government official said. \par \par \uc2  Shiokawa said Tokyo is specifically focusing on the dollar/yen exchange rate, a Cabinet Office official present at the meeting told reporters. \par \par \uc2  When asked by a senior Liberal Democratic Party member if that meant the Finance Ministry will keep \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to weaken the yen, Shiokawa said "we should act according to the situation." \par \par \uc2  Shiokawa's ministry has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  seven times since late May through the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the yen. The dollar has been hurt by a variety of factors, such as weak U.S. stocks and shaky corporate governance. \par \par \uc2  Thursday, the dollar fell below Y117.50 to its lowest levels in more than nine months. \par \par \uc2  BOJ Governor Masaru Hayami, also present at the meeting added that it would be necessary to watch over movements in stock and \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets with "the utmost care." \par \par \uc2  He added that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will continue with its easy monetary policy in order to stabilize the financial markets through the provision of ample liquidity. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par      -By Miyako Takebe, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929;\par miyako.takebe@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020020711dy7b000h3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
