\par\par \b \uc2  Dlr's Gains, Except Vs Yen, May Prompt BOJ  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2  By John Parry \par \uc2 754 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Juli 2002\par 16:55\par \uc2  Dow Jones Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par \par \uc2  NEW YORK -(Dow Jones)- The dollar's moderate advance across the board Thursday - except against the yen - could afford \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  an opportunity to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets with some effect, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategists said. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is getting increasingly likely now, said David Mozina, director of global fixed income and \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  research at Banc of America Securities in New York.  "Without a doubt this is a key level already," Mozina added. \par \par \uc2  The dollar slid below Y117 Thursday morning in New York,  - falling as low as Y116.65 - while the euro also fell to Y115.21 as a wave of speculators tested whether the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Although, both Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Masaru Hayami and Finance Minister Masajuro Shiokawa warned Thursday that further yen strength would be inappropriate for the Japanese economy and that they would move to prevent  a fall in the dollar to Y115, the market continues to press the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  lower. \par \par \uc2  A sustained break of the Y116.85 level could send the dollar towards Y114.00, noted Steven Cox, chief technical analyst with Dow Jones Newswires, a sharp move lower into an  area where few would disagree that Japanese exporters would  be feeling the pinch. \par \par \uc2  The greenback is now in a zone, between Y117.00 and its post-Sept 11 low around Y115.80, where traders warn that broad dollar decline or not, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  becomes a strong possibility. \par \par \uc2  Recently, the finance ministry which acts via the Bank of Japan during such \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 , has  been thwarted in its efforts to weaken the yen against the dollar for all but fleeting periods, by an overwhelming tide  of dollar-negative sentiment. \par \par \uc2  But brief reprieves against most other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , like the dollar's advance against some other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , offer the kind of conditions that the BOJ needs in order for its \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to have the desired effect, U.S.-based strategists said. "The conditions that could "justify" \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  seem to be falling into place," wrote Marc Chandler, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist with HSBC in New York, in a research note Thursday. \par \par \uc2  "The dollar's weakness against the yen cannot be simply  attributed to broad U.S. dollar weakness," while in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  options markets, implied yen volatility is moving higher, which suggests "the speculative nature of the yen gains," Chandler added. \par \par \uc2  Signals from Japanese policymakers have consistently indicated that if the yen firms to the Y115.00 area, that starts to create the risk of choking Japan's fledgling, export-driven recovery. \par \par \uc2  If the dollar dropped below Y115.00, that would then reach the key area that finance ministry and BOJ officials have indicated to the market might trigger \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said Mozina of Banc of America Securities. In that event, `they may come in and stem market concerns," he added. \par \par \uc2  Earlier this week, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategists signaled that the Japanese authorities might seek any reversal of the broad tide of dollar-negative sentiment as a chance to stem the yen's appreciation against the dollar, although the window of opportunity to capitalize on that was fast closing  by midmorning Thursday in New York. \par \par \uc2  Paresh Upadhyaya, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst with Putnam Investments in Boston said Wednesday he expects that Japan's  finance ministry, which acts in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets via the Bank of Japan, "will wait for a small pickup in the dollar - coupled with some signs of a weaker economy in \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which would justify \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market's eyes." \par \par \uc2  As the dollar slipped further against the yen,some of the ideal conditions for the finance ministry to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  were already disappearing, however. Although earlier in the New York day the dollar had been higher against the pound and Swiss franc, it was starting to post losses. The greenback was, however, modestly higher on the session against the euro. \par \par \uc2  At about 10:45 a.m. EDT (1245 GMT) Thursday, the dollar was trading at Y116.85, down from Y117.16 around midday in Europe and down from Y117.61 late Wednesday in New York. The  euro was trading at $0.9873, up from $0.9856 around midday in Europe but moderately down from $0.9889 late Wednesday in  New York. Against the Swiss franc, the dollar was at CHF1.4860, modestly down from CHF1.4869 late Wednesday. Sterling was at $1.5481, up from $1.5462. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    -By John Parry; Dow Jones Newswires\par    john.parry@dowjones.com; 201-938-2096\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020020711dy7b00335\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
