\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dlr gains on euro despite stock slide, slips vs yen. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Andrea Ricci \par \uc2 1,157 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Juli 2002\par 23:19\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NEW YORK, July 10 (Reuters) - The dollar rose against a sluggish euro on Wednesday despite big declines in U.S. stocks but slid more than a third of a percent against an emboldened yen. \par \par \uc2  It was the fourth time in two weeks that Europe's single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rose to within a half cent of parity with the dollar, rising as high as 99.69 cents on Wednesday before running out of steam and receding. \par \par \uc2  The euro eased despite a late-day sell-off in U.S. stocks which took the Dow Jones industrial average down more than 3 percent and the Nasdaq composite down more than 2.5 percent by the close. \par \par \uc2  Over the past few months, the dollar has been on a more or less steady downtrend as international investors, spooked by a seemingly endless parade of corporate scandals, lighten their positions in U.S. equities. \par \par \uc2  The dollar's fortunes - which have been mostly negative - have been strongly correlated with the U.S. stock markets on daily basis, particularly in relation to the euro. \par \par \uc2  Most analysts expect the dollar to come under further pressure and view the euro's recent retrenchment as a pause in its move higher. The euro has gained more than 11 percent against the dollar this year. \par \par \uc2  "Most people, myself included, still think the euro will go higher. It just seems to be running into some resistance," said Tom Benfer, director of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at Bank of Montreal in New York. \par \par \uc2  By late afternoon in New York, the euro was trading at 98.82 cents , down 0.42 percent against the dollar in the session and almost a cent below the day's 99.69 cent high. \par \par \uc2  Options-related activity put pressure on the euro in early U.S. trade, dealers noted. \par \par \uc2  Janna Butland, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Fleet Global Markets, said she expected the euro to resume its upward path. \par \par \uc2  "Speculative flows going into the euro have actually slowed in the past few weeks, meaning the euro's rise has been due not just to speculative flows but also to portfolio adjustment. That's part of the reason why we think that the euro's not reaching parity is just a mild setback, and we don't expect a significant retracement," she said. \par \par \uc2  "Speculative trading can be very fickle, but if it's portfolio flows, it will continue to push the dollar weaker." \par \par \uc2  A Reuters survey of 48 analysts released on Wednesday found that 20 expected the euro to be at $1 or higher by the end of this month. The consensus forecast saw the euro at the one-to-one level in three months time. \par \par \uc2  Sterling fared better than the euro on Wednesday, losing just 0.6 percent against the dollar to trade at $1.5472 . It had hit a fresh 26-month high overnight at 1.5530 after news of a surprise jump in British manufacturing production fueled speculation of higher UK interest rates. \par \par \uc2  The dollar rose 0.32 percent against the Swiss franc to 1.4870 francs . \par \par \uc2  SOFTLY, SOFTLY \par \par \uc2  While the dollar has few friends these days, some analysts caution about getting too bullish on the euro too soon. \par \par \uc2  Thomas Fitzpatrick, technical analyst at Citibank in New York, noted that the euro has been making lower highs of late. "There have been wide trading ranges recently but the euro has been making no further ground," he said. \par \par \uc2  He said a weekly close above 99.90 cents, the high of June 28 and the closest the euro has come to parity, could set the stage for a the euro's move toward $1.0350 or 1.0380. \par \par \uc2  A fall below the 200-week moving average at 97.08 cents would open the way to a lower euro. \par \par \uc2  "It took us five years to get above the 200-week moving average and if we close below that it would be a big alarm bell ringing. If you spend so long trying to achieve something and capitulate so quickly, it is almost as bad a signal as it seemed a good signal in the other direction," he said. \par \par \uc2  Another warning sign for dollar bears was the behavior of the Swiss franc. Fitzpatrick said the Swiss \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had been the leader for much of the dollar's down move this year. But recently, it has stalled. \par \par \uc2  "If everything is as bad as they say (for the dollar), why isn't dollar/Swiss still leading the way?...It may be a warning signal if the leader of the pact is no longer leading." \par \par \uc2  CLEAR SAILING FOR THE YEN \par \par \uc2  The yen meanwhile rose against the dollar to 117.63 yen per dollar by late afternoon, helped by the weaker stock market and unencumbered by even the hint of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The dollar's loss to the yen totaled 0.36 percent. \par \par \uc2  At session highs of 117.40 yen per dollar, the yen was at its highest versus the greenback since late September 2001. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on at least seven days since late May on concerns that a too-steep decline in the dollar against the yen could hurt Japan's export-led economy. \par \par \uc2  The dollar came under renewed selling pressure at the start of the week after Japanese Finance Minister Masajuro Shiokawa said that most policymakers believed the dollar would fall toward 115 yen. \par \par \uc2  He and other monetary officials later attempted to backtrack from that statement, but for many market players, the earlier message stuck. \par \par \uc2  "I don't think anyone is worried about \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  until it gets toward 115," said Vincent Palazzolo, chief dealer at SMBC. "Even if they do try it before, attempts (at \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) are going to be futile until they draw a line in the sand." \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bid prices at 2033GMT. All data taken from Reuters. \par \par \uc2  Calculated from the levels at 4:30 p.m. (20:30 GMT) in the \par \par \uc2  previous New York session. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                       Last  US Close    %      YTD     2001\par                              09 July  Change %Change    Close\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -------------------------------------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Euro/dlr             0.9882   0.9926   -0.44  +10.98   0.8904\par Dlr/yen              117.63   118.06   -0.36  -10.64   131.63\par Euro/yen             116.24   117.20   -0.82   -0.85   117.24\par Dlr/swiss            1.4870   1.4823   +0.32  -10.39   1.6594\par Stg/dlr              1.5472   1.5481   -0.06   +6.40   1.4541\par Dlr/cad              1.5199   1.5117   +0.54   -4.51   1.5917\par Aus/dlr              0.5649   0.5671   -0.39  +10.63   0.5106\par Euro/swiss           1.4696   1.4724   -0.19   -0.57   1.4780\par Euro/stg             0.6386   0.6413   -0.42   +4.30   0.6123\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par All spots\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Tokyo spots\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Europe spots\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Volatilities\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Tokyo \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market info from BOJ\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  World \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  news\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Economic Forecasts...          Official rates...\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \high