\par\par \b \uc2  POLL-Yen to lose ground vs dollar in coming year. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Joanne Russell \par \uc2 615 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Juli 2002\par 13:31\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, July 10 (Reuters) - Analysts expect the dollar to remain under pressure against the yen in coming weeks but say the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  will then be held back by poor economic fundamentals, according to a Reuters survey. In a poll of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategists carried out from July 8 to 10, the mid-range of 48 forecasts showed the yen at 119.00 per dollar in one month's time from around 117.80 at 1030 GMT on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Analysts then saw the yen at 120.00 in three months' time, 120.83 in six months and 122.00 one year out. \par \par \uc2  "We remain yen bears for the long-run," said Arjun Mittal at American Express in London. "We still think Japan has unresolved structural problems, low productivity growth... problems in its banking system. \par \par \uc2  "At the moment it's just dollar weakness across the board. Our view is the U.S. will have a tough six months but 2003 will get better, both for the economy and for U.S. markets." \par \par \uc2  The dollar dropped to 117.65 yen in early European trade on Wednesday, its lowest since September 27, undermined by losses in U.S. stocks and jitters over U.S. corporate accounting. \par \par \uc2  The greenback has come under renewed selling pressure since the start of the week after weekend comments by Japanese Finance Minister Masajuro Shiokawa that world financial authorities believed a weakening of the dollar was in progress and that it could fall to levels hit immediately after September 11. \par \par \uc2  Senior Finance Ministry official Zembei Mizoguchi talked up the dollar on Wednesday, calling its overnight fall below 118 yen "not a favourable situation" and giving now customary hints of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell yen for dollars on at least seven days since late May to counter the yen's rise, which it fears could derail the nation's fragile export-led recovery. \par \par \uc2  UNDER PRESSURE \par \par \uc2  "While the yen is set to benefit from broad based dollar weakness in the short term, long-term we remain bearish on the yen," said Geraldine Concagh at Allied Irish Bank in Dublin. \par \par \uc2  The range of dollar/yen forecasts in the survey on a 12-month view was 105.00 to 145.00. \par \par \uc2  Concerns about the Japanese economy, the world's second largest, will weigh on the yen, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  "The downward trend in dollar/yen looks to remain throughout the month of July, but is likely to lose steam as reform efforts in Japan have been watered down... which should once again place pressure on the yen going forward," said Tim Mazanec at Investors Bank and Trust in Boston. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Japan has already reduced interest rates to almost zero to help the economy along. \par \par \uc2  Some recent economic news has been positive. Japan's economy grew at an annualised rate of 5.7 percent in the first three months of the year, drawing a line under three straight quarters of contraction. \par \par \uc2  But personal consumption, the biggest part of the economy, remains in the doldrums, and unemployment stood at 5.4 percent of the workforce in May, just below a postwar high of 5.5 percent in December. \par \par \uc2  "The fact that domestic demand remains so weak in Japan calls for a weak exchange rate to boost exports and bring Japan out of a 10-year recession," said Rui Constantino at Banco Santander de Negocios in Lisbon. \par \par \uc2  Implicit cross rates from the poll showed euro/yen at 117.48 in one month's time, 120.00 in three, 121.25 in six and 121.98 in 12 months, according to the mid-range forecasts. \par \par \uc2  . \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020710dy7a00mul\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
