\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  talks up dollar, repeats  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  hints. \b0\par\par\uc2 261 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Juli 2002\par 10:23\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, July 10 (Reuters) - Senior Finance Ministry official Zembei Mizoguchi resumed Japan's rearguard attempt to talk up the dollar on Wednesday, calling its overnight fall below 118 yen "unfavourable" and giving now customary hints of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Worried that the yen's strength could hurt \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's tentative economic recovery, which is led by exports, Japanese authorities have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market at least seven times over the past two months, selling yen and buying dollars. \par \par \uc2  The dollar fell to a 10-month low of 117.72 yen in overnight trading, down more than 13 percent from the beginning of April and its lowest rate since September last year. \par \par \uc2  Asked about the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's latest weakening, Mizoguchi told reporters at the ministry: "It is not a favourable situation." \par \par \uc2  He said rapid moves in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market were undesirable, and that Japanese authorities were ready to take action if necessary. \par \par \uc2  By mid-morning the dollar was barely holding above 118 yen, and dealers said it was supported only by fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "There is absolutely no change in our position that we will take appropriate action if needed," said Mizoguchi, the head of the ministry's international bureau. \par \par \uc2  But when reminded that Japanese authorities had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in recent weeks when the dollar was around current levels, Mizoguchi only said he would not comment on specific levels. \par \par \uc2  Japan takes the stance that \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  should reflect economic fundamentals and dislikes rapid movements in rates. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020710dy7a00h51\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
