\par\par \b \uc2  Euro Nears Parity With Dollar As Bush Speech Fails to Impress \b0\par\par\uc2  By Tyler Lifton \par \uc2 867 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Juli 2002\par 00:48\par \uc2  Dow Jones Business News \par \uc2 DJON\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Dow Jones Newswires \par \par \uc2  NEW YORK -- The dollar weakened across the board Tuesday, sinking to its lowest level against the yen in almost ten months and once again coming close to parity with the euro, as a much anticipated speech by President Bush on corporate accountability failed to spark a rally on Wall Street. \par \par \uc2  Speaking in lower Manhattan, Mr. Bush ordered the creation of a Corporate Fraud Task Force that would combine the efforts of several federal agencies, called for increased jail time for corrupt executives and proposed an additional $100 million in funding for the Securities and Exchange Commission. The speech came amid a crisis of confidence in corporate America that has done significant damage to U.S. capital markets and underpinned the dollar's decline. \par \par \uc2  But Mr. Bush's remarks were given a tepid review by market professionals, doing little to dent the wave of negative sentiment currently clouding the dollar. According to Karen Petrou, managing partner at Federal Financial Analytics in Washington D.C., the speech didn't properly address the issues of transparency or market integrity. \par \par \uc2  And threatening longer jail time -- and other penalties -- for white collar crime -- one of the key aspects of Mr. Bush's speech -- doesn't "have much preventative value," Ms. Petrou said. \par \par \uc2  While Mr. Bush's speech did offer some concrete proposals, "in the near term, it doesn't eliminate, nor could it, a lot of the risk out there," said Jay Bryson, a global economist at Wachovia Securities in Charlotte, N.C. What's more, "if you believe the stock market is still overvalued, it doesn't do anything to address that problem," he added. \par \par \uc2  With nothing to grasp onto from the Bush speech, traders pushed the dollar to within half a cent of parity with the euro, while shoving it below 118 yen against the yen, to its weakest point against the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  since Sept. 27, 2001. That placed it well below the range that has prompted multiple \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  since late May. As a result, traders are on the lookout for more \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as the Japanese government seeks to check the yen's strength fearing it could derail Japan's fragile economic recovery. \par \par \uc2  "The market's just holding its breath and waiting to see what Shiokawa does," said Jason Bonanca, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at Credit Suisse First Boston in New York, referring to the potential for the MOF to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on behalf of the yen during Tokyo business hours. \par \par \uc2  Comments by Japanese Finance Minister Masajuro Shiokawa in recent days have been interpreted by market players as a growing resignation by Japan towards a stronger yen, despite the problems that might create for \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's exporters. \par \par \uc2  But the threat of another \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  still looms, given the size of the yen's ascent versus the dollar of late. "We are interested in the way \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates move, and if there is excessive speed [in moves] we must think of ways of dealing with that," Mr. Shiokawa said Monday in Tokyo. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, even disappointing economic news out of Germany couldn't stop the euro from appreciating against the dollar. German industrial data showed that output declined by 1.3% on the month in May, instead of rising by 0.3% as forecast. April output was also revised to a decline of 0.2%, from a rise of 0.2%. \par \par \uc2  The German unemployment rate remained at 9.5% in June, as expected. However, the number of people out of work rose by 39,000 on the month, more than the 30,000 that had been forecast. The International Monetary Fund also downgraded its forecast for German growth this year. \par \par \uc2  But regardless of anything negative from the euro zone, it is more pessimism about the dollar than optimism for European growth that is driving the relationship between the two \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the moment. \par \par \uc2  "This isn't about Europe as a good buy," said Michael Woolfolk, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Bank of New York. "It just so happens that capital flow is leaving the U.S. at a more rapid pace than it is leaving Europe." \par \par \uc2  Late in the day, the euro was trading at 99.34 U.S. cents, up from 98.67 cents late Monday. The dollar was listed at 117.94 yen, down from 118.57 yen late Monday. Against the Swiss franc, the dollar was at 1.4825 francs, down from 1.4885 francs the day prior, while sterling was at $1.5482, up from $1.5373 Monday. \par \par \uc2  Among other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the dollar had a particularly weak day against its Canadian counterpart, falling to 1.5120 Canadian dollars late Tuesday, versus 1.5217 dollars late Monday. That made it the biggest mover in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Tuesday, said CSFB's Mr. Bonanca, who pegged the move to momentum gathering behind the "ever widening interest-rate differential in Canada's favor ... [and] really robust economic numbers" coming out of Canada. \par \par \uc2  -- Miyako Takebe in Tokyo contributed to this report. \par \par \uc2  Write to Tyler Lifton at tyler.lifton@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  Copyright (c) 2002 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Dokument djon000020020709dy79005v6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
