\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar takes beating on Merck, Reliant accounting. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Sumeet Desai \par \uc2 592 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Juli 2002\par 12:19\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, July 8 (Reuters) - The dollar sank against major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday, hit by yet more news of U.S. accounting irregularities and the Japanese finance minister's suggestion that policymakers were prepared for a decline in the greenback. \par \par \uc2  The dollar bounced last week from steep losses which had brought it to within a whisker of parity with the euro but accounting concerns at drugmaker Merck and energy trader Reliant Resources pushed it down sharply on Monday. \par \par \uc2  "The bear market in the dollar is supporting all the major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Most of the focus is on the recast U.S. earnings statements," said Monica Fan, senior strategist at BankAmerica. \par \par \uc2  By 1005 GMT the dollar was 1.3 percent down at $.0.9855 per euro, erasing much of last week's gains and turning back towards its two-year low of $0.9990 set at the end of June. \par \par \uc2  The greenback stood less than half a yen off a recent nine-month low, at 118.70, and had also shed more than one percent against the Swiss franc. \par \par \uc2  U.S. ACCOUNTING \par \par \uc2  The Wall Street Journal reported on Monday that drugs giant Merck & Co had recorded $12.4 billion in revenues from its pharmacy-benefits unit during the past three years that the subsidiary had never collected. \par \par \uc2  This compounded news late on Friday that Reliant Resources was restating its accounts for the past three years, erasing $7.9 billion in revenues. U.S. stock futures were lining up for steep losses at Monday's Wall Street opening. \par \par \uc2  "The dollar's weakness is clearly due to more concerns about U.S. accounting irregularities," said Ryan Shea, senior international economist at Bank One. \par \par \uc2  "There is also caution coming into the U.S. second quarter earnings season. The whole U.S. corporate sector is under the spotlight and it's a pretty negative spotlight given that the current account deficit continues to require funding." \par \par \uc2  The dollar has come under pressure in recent months as the collapse of energy giant Enron and details of accounting irregularities at long distance carrier WorldCom have raised questions about the appeal of U.S. assets. \par \par \uc2  Traders also said dollar bulls were disappointed after the greenback failed to extend a mini-rally after Friday's jump in U.S. share prices. \par \par \uc2  JAPAN \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, Japanese Finance Minister Masajuro Shiokawa said world financial authorities believed the dollar could fall to around 115 yen, levels hit just after the September 11 attacks on the U.S. \par \par \uc2  Traders were puzzled as the comments seemed to fly in the face of Japan's recent efforts to keep the yen from strengthening so as not to hurt its exporters. \par \par \uc2  But Shiokawa did add: "I maintain that even if (the dollar) is heading to that level, a certain amount of time needs to be spent and it should not reach that level abruptly." \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy dollars for yen on at least seven occasions in May and June. Last month, it even enlisted the U.S. Federal Reserve and European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to act as its agent to sell yen in the market. \par \par \uc2  Traders said they remained wary that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  could still \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  again, especially if the dollar approached its recent nine-month low of 118.36. \par \par \uc2  In its annual report, the Bank for International Settlements (BIS), the central bankers' bank, said the dollar was overvalued against the euro when measured by purchasing power parity but it was hard to say by how much. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020708dy7800l59\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
