\par\par \b \uc2  Asian gold up in afternoon, TOCOM off in active trade. \b0\par\par\uc2 402 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Juli 2002\par 09:42\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  HONG KONG, July 8 (Reuters) - Spot gold crawled steadily higher in Asia on Monday, launched initially by TOCOM-related trade, then powered by nervous Europeans covering shorts ahead of New York's return from its four-day holiday, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  An appreciating yen or a depreciating dollar will keep upward pressure on the yellow metal, but the trend could be truncated at any time by \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the yen or changes to the short-term dollar-gold correlation. \par \par \uc2  Spot gold was trading at US$311.50/2.00 an ounce at 0600 GMT, higher than the open in Hong Kong at US$310.70/1.20 and London's last quoted US$311.25/1.75. \par \par \uc2  "I see some room on the upside... to possibly 118.50, although the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  will keep \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Gordon Cheung, director of Precious Metals Trading at Mitsui Bussan in Hong Kong. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Japan's attempts to halt the appreciation of the yen last week were largely unsuccessful, but the efforts did stimulate intra-day volatility in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  and precious metals' markets. \par \par \uc2  The near-term outlook was still downward for gold. \par \par \uc2  "There are too many bears around the market," said Cheung. \par \par \uc2  Those bearish bullion investors were expecting another good performance by the Dow Jones Industrial Average which bounced 3.6 percent on Friday as well as better economic data in coming weeks. \par \par \uc2  Gold bulls, on the other hand, warned that more revelations of corporate difficulties were likely in the coming week. \par \par \uc2  "Apart from the disclosure of second-quarter earnings, executives will be making comments about the business outlook," said Maxell Mak, analyst at Hing Fung Goldsmiths and Refinery. \par \par \uc2  TOCOM June 2003 was trading 14 yen lower at 1,187 yen on very active trade of 61,184 contracts. The yen strengthened against the dollar to a day high of 118.75/8.89 yen to the dollar at 0700. \par \par \uc2  Hong Kong tael gold , which is traded on the Chinese Gold and Silver Exchange, ended the morning session at HK$2,892, up from the open at HK$2,886. \par \par \uc2  A tael is equal to 1.203 ounces of gold. \par \par \uc2  Kilogold ended the morning unchanged at HK$77.90 a gramme. \par \par \uc2  Spot silver was higher at US$4.92/4.94 an ounce, up from US$4.90/4.92. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020708dy7800fr8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
