\par\par \b \uc2  Japan/Take  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  Steps -2: Fukuda Spins Shiokawa Y115 Remark \b0\par\par\uc2 262 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Juli 2002\par 09:27\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  TOKYO (Nikkei/Dow Jones)--The Japanese government's top spokesman sought Friday to quash speculation that Finance Minister Masajuro Shiokawa was retreating on the authorities' commitment to curbing the yen's rise. \par \par \uc2  "The meaning was we will craft measures if the yen appreciates from here," said Chief Cabinet Secretary Yasuo Fukuda. \par \par \uc2  Overnight, Shiokawa told reporters on a trip to Copenhagen, "There is some speculation the dollar could go to Y115," as it did after the Sept. 11 terrorist attacks on the U.S. "We want to avoid it going there." \par \par \uc2  Shiokawa's remark fueled speculation that Japan was abandoning Y120 as a defense for the dollar, a line that Tokyo was thought to be eyeing but which has already been breached. \par \par \uc2  The dollar hit the Y115 level on Sept. 20, falling from the Y121 level prior to the Sept. 11 terrorist attacks. The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has recently traded around the Y120 level, compared with levels above Y130 three months ago. \par \par \uc2  Reflecting the authorities' discomfort over the yen's recent sharp rise, Chief Cabinet Secretary Fukuda said, "Sharp \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves are undesirable." \par \par \uc2  Since May 22, the Finance Ministry has conducted seven rounds of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  through the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the yen's rapid rise from snuffing out the nation's budding export-led recovery. \par \par \uc2  Last Friday, Japan sold yen via the U.S. Federal Reserve and the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the first time in its recent series of \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    -By Tokyo Bureau; Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020020705dy75000ej\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 (foreign exchange or fx or forex or currenc*) and (interven* or operation*) and (japan near10 interven*) and (rst=trtw or rst=tprw or rst=tdjw) and (central bank or ministry of finance or treasury ministry or monetary authority)\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\row } \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Datum\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 01/01/1995 bis 21/08/2023\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\row } \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdr